Because the greatest gift cyberattackers have ever received is smarter AI, and right now only one side is armed.

Arm the defenders.

We're thrilled to invest in First Person Labs.

For personal agents to become useful in everyday life, they need a total understanding of you. That creates something extraordinarily sensitive: a model of your relationships, priorities, habits, and intentions. We believe you should be in total control of it.

@FirstPersonLabs’ product, Second, builds a continuously updated model of you that can serve context to the agents you choose. It runs on your device by default, and you control what other applications and agents can access.

@kenziyuliu and @erikchi understand both how AI learns about people and how to build systems that keep people in control. Ken's research at Stanford and Google DeepMind focused on AI and data privacy. Erik's work at Michigan focused on network security, privacy, and censorship resistance.

Congrats to Ken, Erik and the First Person Labs team!

